WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.165 --> 00:00:05.335
NARRATOR: Our story
opens with revolution.

00:00:07.837 --> 00:00:09.872
After decades of cold war,

00:00:09.906 --> 00:00:13.142
the mighty Soviet
empire is collapsing.

00:00:13.876 --> 00:00:16.646
MAN: The wall is
effectively down.

00:00:16.946 --> 00:00:19.349
NARRATOR: Just weeks
before the 90s begin,

00:00:19.382 --> 00:00:21.484
the most famous symbol
of the political divide

00:00:21.517 --> 00:00:25.388
between east and
west is toppled.

00:00:26.255 --> 00:00:29.058
CHUNG: We as boomers lived
under the threat of nuclear war.

00:00:29.092 --> 00:00:31.527
We lived with the Cold War.

00:00:31.561 --> 00:00:35.798
The Berlin Wall was the
symbol of all of that.

00:00:36.265 --> 00:00:37.934
CHUNG (over TV): Today was the
beginning of the end of

00:00:37.967 --> 00:00:40.470
what they call
the wall of shame.

00:00:41.904 --> 00:00:43.773
CHUNG: It was a glorious moment.

00:00:43.806 --> 00:00:46.242
It was like a street party.

00:00:46.275 --> 00:00:48.611
MAN (over TV): Until yesterday
the wall was a symbol of

00:00:48.645 --> 00:00:50.613
Cold War fear and loathing.

00:00:50.647 --> 00:00:53.549
Tonight it's the scene for
a celebration of freedom,

00:00:53.583 --> 00:00:56.085
peace and love.

00:00:56.119 --> 00:00:58.688
NARRATOR: As political shock
waves echo across Europe

00:00:58.721 --> 00:01:03.059
the world watches as the
Soviet super power collapses.

00:01:03.593 --> 00:01:06.229
MAN (over TV): The exuberance,
the delight, the passion,

00:01:06.262 --> 00:01:08.064
they are all tangible.

00:01:08.097 --> 00:01:11.367
40 years of Stalinist
oppression crumbling.

00:01:12.502 --> 00:01:15.538
NARRATOR: And in December 1991,
communist leader

00:01:15.571 --> 00:01:20.510
Mikhail Gorbachev declares
the end of the Soviet Union.

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:25.615
The Cold War which sparked fears
of global apocalypse is over.

00:01:30.319 --> 00:01:32.455
CLINTON: Russia's strategic
nuclear missiles soon will

00:01:32.488 --> 00:01:35.124
no longer be pointed at
the United States.

00:01:35.158 --> 00:01:37.627
Nor will we
point ours at them.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:40.863
(applause)

00:01:40.897 --> 00:01:43.199
NARRATOR: As lifelong
enemies join forces,

00:01:43.232 --> 00:01:46.736
they open up bold new frontiers.

00:01:47.637 --> 00:01:50.006
CLINTON: Instead of
building weapons in space,

00:01:50.039 --> 00:01:52.775
Russian scientists will
help us to build

00:01:52.809 --> 00:01:57.180
the International Space Station.

00:01:57.213 --> 00:01:59.682
(applause)

00:01:59.782 --> 00:02:02.652
KURT: The space race had
been part of the Cold War,

00:02:02.685 --> 00:02:05.088
especially in the early
days it was all about

00:02:05.121 --> 00:02:07.390
we gotta get to the moon
before the Soviets.

00:02:07.423 --> 00:02:08.858
MAN (over TV): They've got the
flag up, you can see the

00:02:08.891 --> 00:02:10.193
stars and stripes.

00:02:10.226 --> 00:02:15.098
KURT: It made sense in a
symbolic way to to show that

00:02:15.131 --> 00:02:21.037
the old Cold War including this
ferocious space race was done.

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:23.339
MAN: This is an historic moment
that I'm just very excited.

00:02:23.372 --> 00:02:26.342
Mr. Kopchev I wanna
give you a hug.

00:02:26.375 --> 00:02:28.511
(laughter, applause)

00:02:30.646 --> 00:02:33.683
NARRATOR: With grand designs
for a high tech future,

00:02:33.716 --> 00:02:37.920
construction starts on a project
of cosmic scale and ambition.

00:02:39.088 --> 00:02:43.326
BILL: The purpose of the ISS is
to be a laboratory in space.

00:02:43.359 --> 00:02:47.563
It's the largest international
cooperative science program

00:02:47.597 --> 00:02:50.233
that we've ever seen.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.403
15 nations managed by five
separate space agencies,

00:02:55.138 --> 00:02:58.441
all contributing to make
this laboratory a reality.

00:02:58.474 --> 00:03:00.376
NARRATOR: And as mission
training begins in

00:03:00.409 --> 00:03:02.411
Moscow and Houston,

00:03:02.445 --> 00:03:05.414
for a launch that will
herald the new millennium,

00:03:05.448 --> 00:03:10.253
humanity contemplates
its destiny.

00:03:10.286 --> 00:03:11.954
BILL: One of the biggest
questions that the space station

00:03:11.988 --> 00:03:14.624
is trying to help answer is,

00:03:14.657 --> 00:03:17.860
is earth the only spot
in the whole universe

00:03:17.894 --> 00:03:19.529
that we can reside or

00:03:19.562 --> 00:03:22.832
do we have the capacity to
live and work elsewhere?

